    <article class="docs-prose">
      <h1 id="update-completing-the-y-stream-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Completing the y-stream cluster update<a href="#update-completing-the-y-stream-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">Complete the following steps to perform a y-stream cluster update.</p>
      <h2 id="update-acknowledging-update-for-eus-eus-y-stream_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Acknowledging the control plane only or y-stream update<a href="#update-acknowledging-update-for-eus-eus-y-stream_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">When you update to all versions from 4.11 and later, you must manually acknowledge that the update can continue.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Before you acknowledge the update, verify that you are not using any of the Kubernetes APIs that are removed from the version you are updating to. For example, in OpenShift Container Platform 4.17, there are no API removals. See "Kubernetes API removals" for more information.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have verified that APIs for all of the applications running on your cluster are compatible with the next Y-stream release of OpenShift Container Platform. For more details about compatibility, see "Verifying cluster API versions between update versions".</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Check the cluster update status to determine if administrative acknowledgment is required by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc adm upgrade"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>If the cluster update does not complete successfully, more details about the update failure are provided in the <code>Reason</code> and <code>Message</code> sections.</p>
      <p>Example output:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"Cluster version is 4.15.45\n\nUpgradeable=False\n\n  Reason: MultipleReasons\n  Message: Cluster should not be upgraded between minor versions for multiple reasons: AdminAckRequired,ResourceDeletesInProgress\n  * Kubernetes 1.29 and therefore OpenShift 4.16 remove several APIs which require admin consideration. Please see the knowledge article https://access.redhat.com/articles/7031404 for details and instructions.\n  * Cluster minor level upgrades are not allowed while resource deletions are in progress; resources=PrometheusRule \"openshift-kube-apiserver/kube-apiserver-recording-rules\"\n\nReleaseAccepted=False\n\n  Reason: PreconditionChecks\n  Message: Preconditions failed for payload loaded version=\"4.16.34\" image=\"quay.io/openshift-release-dev/ocp-release@sha256:41bb08c560f6db5039ccdf242e590e8b23049b5eb31e1c4f6021d1d520b353b8\": Precondition \"ClusterVersionUpgradeable\" failed because of \"MultipleReasons\": Cluster should not be upgraded between minor versions for multiple reasons: AdminAckRequired,ResourceDeletesInProgress\n  * Kubernetes 1.29 and therefore OpenShift 4.16 remove several APIs which require admin consideration. Please see the knowledge article https://access.redhat.com/articles/7031404 for details and instructions.\n  * Cluster minor level upgrades are not allowed while resource deletions are in progress; resources=PrometheusRule \"openshift-kube-apiserver/kube-apiserver-recording-rules\"\n\nUpstream is unset, so the cluster will use an appropriate default.\nChannel: eus-4.16 (available channels: candidate-4.15, candidate-4.16, eus-4.16, fast-4.15, fast-4.16, stable-4.15, stable-4.16)\n\nRecommended updates:\n\n  VERSION     IMAGE\n  4.16.34     quay.io/openshift-release-dev/ocp-release@sha256:41bb08c560f6db5039ccdf242e590e8b23049b5eb31e1c4f6021d1d520b353b8"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>In this example, a linked Red Hat Knowledgebase article (<a href="https://access.redhat.com/articles/7031404">Preparing to upgrade to OpenShift Container Platform 4.16</a>) provides more detail about verifying API compatibility between releases.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify the update by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get configmap admin-acks -n openshift-config -o json | jq .data"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>If the acknowledgment was successful, the output shows the acknowledged API removals for each update:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"{\n  \"ack-4.14-kube-1.28-api-removals-in-4.15\": \"true\",\n  \"ack-4.15-kube-1.29-api-removals-in-4.16\": \"true\"\n}"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>In this example, the cluster is updated from version 4.14 to 4.15, and then from 4.15 to 4.16 in a Control Plane Only update.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul><li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/updating/preparing_for_updates/updating-cluster-prepare#kube-api-removals_updating-cluster-prepare">Kubernetes API removals</a></li></ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="update-starting-the-cluster-update_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Starting the cluster update<a href="#update-starting-the-cluster-update_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">When updating from one y-stream release to the next, you must ensure that the intermediate z-stream releases are also compatible.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You can verify that you are updating to a viable release by running the <code>oc adm upgrade</code> command. The <code>oc adm upgrade</code> command lists the compatible update releases.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Start the update:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc adm upgrade --to=4.15.33"} lang="terminal" />
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <ul>
          <li><strong>Control plane only update</strong>: Ensure you point to the interim &lt;y+1&gt; release path</li>
          <li><strong>Y-stream update</strong> - Ensure you use the correct &lt;y.z&gt; release that follows the Kubernetes <a href="https://kubernetes.io/releases/version-skew-policy/">version skew policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Z-stream update</strong> - Verify that there are no problems moving to that specific release</li>
          </ul>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <CodeBlock code={"Requested update to <version>"} lang="terminal" />
      <ul><li></li></ul>
      <p>where: <code>&lt;version&gt;</code>:: Specifies the version number for your particular update, such as <code>4.15.33</code>.</p>
      </li>
      </ol>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul><li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/post_installation_configuration/day_2_core_cnf_clusters/updating/update-api#update-selecting-the-target-release_update-api">Selecting the target release</a></li></ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="update-monitoring-the-cluster-update_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Monitoring the cluster update<a href="#update-monitoring-the-cluster-update_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You should check the cluster health often during the update. Check for the node status, cluster Operators status and failed pods.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Monitor the cluster update. For example, to monitor the cluster update from version 4.14 to 4.15, run the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ watch \"oc get clusterversion; echo; oc get co | head -1; oc get co | grep 4.14; oc get co | grep 4.15; echo; oc get no; echo; oc get po -A | grep -E -iv 'running|complete'\""} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME      VERSION   AVAILABLE   PROGRESSING   SINCE   STATUS\nversion   4.14.34   True        True          4m6s    Working towards 4.15.33: 111 of 873 done (12% complete), waiting on kube-apiserver\n\nNAME                           VERSION   AVAILABLE   PROGRESSING   DEGRADED   SINCE   MESSAGE\nauthentication                 4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\nbaremetal                      4.14.34   True        False         False      4d23h\ncloud-controller-manager       4.14.34   True        False         False      4d23h\ncloud-credential               4.14.34   True        False         False      4d23h\ncluster-autoscaler             4.14.34   True        False         False      4d23h\nconsole                        4.14.34   True        False         False      4d22h\n\n...\n\nstorage                        4.14.34   True        False         False      4d23h\nconfig-operator                4.15.33   True        False         False      4d23h\netcd                           4.15.33   True        False         False      4d23h\n\nNAME           STATUS   ROLES                  AGE     VERSION\nctrl-plane-0   Ready    control-plane,master   4d23h   v1.27.15+6147456\nctrl-plane-1   Ready    control-plane,master   4d23h   v1.27.15+6147456\nctrl-plane-2   Ready    control-plane,master   4d23h   v1.27.15+6147456\nworker-0       Ready    mcp-1,worker           4d23h   v1.27.15+6147456\nworker-1       Ready    mcp-2,worker           4d23h   v1.27.15+6147456\n\nNAMESPACE               NAME                       READY   STATUS              RESTARTS   AGE\nopenshift-marketplace   redhat-marketplace-rf86t   0/1     ContainerCreating   0          0s"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <p>During the update the <code>watch</code> command cycles through one or several of the cluster Operators at a time, providing a status of the Operator update in the <code>MESSAGE</code> column.</p>
      <p>When the cluster Operators update process is complete, each control plane nodes is rebooted, one at a time.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>During this part of the update, messages are reported that state cluster Operators are being updated again or are in a degraded state. This is because the control plane node is offline while it reboots nodes.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p>As soon as the last control plane node reboot is complete, the cluster version is displayed as updated.</p>
      <p>When the control plane update is complete a message such as the following is displayed. This example shows an update completed to the intermediate y-stream release.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME      VERSION   AVAILABLE   PROGRESSING   SINCE   STATUS\nversion   4.15.33   True        False         28m     Cluster version is 4.15.33\n\nNAME                         VERSION   AVAILABLE   PROGRESSING   DEGRADED   SINCE   MESSAGE\nauthentication               4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d\nbaremetal                    4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d\ncloud-controller-manager     4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d1h\ncloud-credential             4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d1h\ncluster-autoscaler           4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d\nconfig-operator              4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d\nconsole                      4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d\n\n...\n\nservice-ca                   4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d\nstorage                      4.15.33   True        False         False\t  5d\n\nNAME           STATUS   ROLES                  AGE   VERSION\nctrl-plane-0   Ready    control-plane,master   5d    v1.28.13+2ca1a23\nctrl-plane-1   Ready    control-plane,master   5d    v1.28.13+2ca1a23\nctrl-plane-2   Ready    control-plane,master   5d    v1.28.13+2ca1a23\nworker-0       Ready    mcp-1,worker           5d    v1.28.13+2ca1a23\nworker-1       Ready    mcp-2,worker           5d    v1.28.13+2ca1a23"} lang="terminal" />
      <h2 id="update-updating-the-olm-operators_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Updating the OLM Operators<a href="#update-updating-the-olm-operators_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Software needs to vetted before it is loaded onto a production cluster. Production clusters are also quite often configured in disconnected network, which means that they are not always directly connected to the internet. Because the clusters are in a disconnected network, the OpenShift Container Platform Operators are configured for manual update during installation so that new versions can be managed on a cluster-by-cluster basis. Complete the following procedure to move the Operators to the newer versions.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Check to see which Operators need to be updated:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get installplan -A | grep -E 'APPROVED|false'"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAMESPACE           NAME            CSV                                               APPROVAL   APPROVED\nmetallb-system      install-nwjnh   metallb-operator.v4.16.0-202409202304             Manual     false\nopenshift-nmstate   install-5r7wr   kubernetes-nmstate-operator.4.16.0-202409251605   Manual     false"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Patch the <code>InstallPlan</code> resources for those Operators:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch installplan -n metallb-system install-nwjnh --type merge --patch \\\n'{\"spec\":{\"approved\":true}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"installplan.operators.coreos.com/install-nwjnh patched"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Monitor the namespace by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get all -n metallb-system"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                                                       READY   STATUS              RESTARTS   AGE\npod/metallb-operator-controller-manager-69b5f884c-8bp22    0/1     ContainerCreating   0          4s\npod/metallb-operator-controller-manager-77895bdb46-bqjdx   1/1     Running             0          4m1s\npod/metallb-operator-webhook-server-5d9b968896-vnbhk       0/1     ContainerCreating   0          4s\npod/metallb-operator-webhook-server-d76f9c6c8-57r4w        1/1     Running             0          4m1s\n\n...\n\nNAME                                                             DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-controller-manager-69b5f884c    1         1         0       4s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-controller-manager-77895bdb46   1         1         1       4m1s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-controller-manager-99b76f88     0         0         0       4m40s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-webhook-server-5d9b968896       1         1         0       4s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-webhook-server-6f7dbfdb88       0         0         0       4m40s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-webhook-server-d76f9c6c8        1         1         1       4m1s"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <p>When the update is complete, the required pods should be in a <code>Running</code> state, and the required <code>ReplicaSet</code> resources should be ready:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                                                      READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\npod/metallb-operator-controller-manager-69b5f884c-8bp22   1/1     Running   0          25s\npod/metallb-operator-webhook-server-5d9b968896-vnbhk      1/1     Running   0          25s\n\n...\n\nNAME                                                             DESIRED   CURRENT   READY   AGE\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-controller-manager-69b5f884c    1         1         1       25s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-controller-manager-77895bdb46   0         0         0       4m22s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-webhook-server-5d9b968896       1         1         1       25s\nreplicaset.apps/metallb-operator-webhook-server-d76f9c6c8        0         0         0       4m22s"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify that the Operators do not need to be updated for a second time:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get installplan -A | grep -E 'APPROVED|false'"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>There should be no output returned.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Sometimes you have to approve an update twice because some Operators have interim z-stream release versions that need to be installed before the final version.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <section class="related-resources _additional-resources">
      <p class="related-resources-title">Additional resources</p>
      <ul><li><a href="/openshift-docs-markdown/post_installation_configuration/day_2_core_cnf_clusters/updating/update-completing-the-control-plane-only-update#update-updating-the-worker-nodes_completing-the-update">Updating the worker nodes</a></li></ul>
      </section>
      <h2 id="update-updating-the-worker-nodes_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Updating the worker nodes<a href="#update-updating-the-worker-nodes_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You upgrade the worker nodes after you have updated the control plane by unpausing the relevant <code>mcp</code> groups you created. Unpausing the <code>mcp</code> group starts the upgrade process for the worker nodes in that group. Each of the worker nodes in the cluster reboot to upgrade to the new EUS, y-stream or z-stream version as required.</p>
      <p>In the case of control plane only upgrades, note that when a worker node is updated it will only require one reboot and will jump &lt;y+2&gt;-release versions. This is a feature that was added to decrease the amount of time that it takes to upgrade large bare-metal clusters.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>This is a potential holding point. You can have a cluster version that is fully supported to run in production with the control plane that is updated to a new EUS release while the worker nodes are at a &lt;y-2&gt;-release. This allows large clusters to upgrade in steps across several maintenance windows.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      You can check how many nodes are managed in an <code>mcp</code> group. Run the following command to get the list of <code>mcp</code> groups:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get mcp"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME     CONFIG                                             UPDATED   UPDATING   DEGRADED   MACHINECOUNT   READYMACHINECOUNT   UPDATEDMACHINECOUNT   DEGRADEDMACHINECOUNT   AGE\nmaster   rendered-master-c9a52144456dbff9c9af9c5a37d1b614   True      False      False      3              3                   3                     0                      36d\nmcp-1    rendered-mcp-1-07fe50b9ad51fae43ed212e84e1dcc8e    False     False      False      1              0                   0                     0                      47h\nmcp-2    rendered-mcp-2-07fe50b9ad51fae43ed212e84e1dcc8e    False     False      False      1              0                   0                     0                      47h\nworker   rendered-worker-f1ab7b9a768e1b0ac9290a18817f60f0   True      False      False      0              0                   0                     0                      36d"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You decide how many <code>mcp</code> groups to upgrade at a time. This depends on how many pods can be taken down at a time and how your pod disruption budget and anti-affinity settings are configured.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      <li>
      Get the list of nodes in the cluster:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get nodes"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME           STATUS   ROLES                  AGE    VERSION\nctrl-plane-0   Ready    control-plane,master   5d8h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nctrl-plane-1   Ready    control-plane,master   5d8h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nctrl-plane-2   Ready    control-plane,master   5d8h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nworker-0       Ready    mcp-1,worker           5d8h   v1.27.15+6147456\nworker-1       Ready    mcp-2,worker           5d8h   v1.27.15+6147456"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Confirm the <code>MachineConfigPool</code> groups that are paused:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get mcp -o json | jq -r '[\"MCP\",\"Paused\"], [\"---\",\"------\"], (.items[] | [(.metadata.name), (.spec.paused)]) | @tsv' | grep -v worker"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"MCP     Paused\n---     ------\nmaster  false\nmcp-1   true\nmcp-2   true"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Each <code>MachineConfigPool</code> can be unpaused independently. Therefore, if a maintenance window runs out of time other MCPs do not need to be unpaused immediately. The cluster is supported to run with some worker nodes still at &lt;y-2&gt;-release version.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      <li>
      Unpause the required <code>mcp</code> group to begin the upgrade:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc patch mcp/mcp-1 --type merge --patch '{\"spec\":{\"paused\":false}}'"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"machineconfigpool.machineconfiguration.openshift.io/mcp-1 patched"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Confirm that the required <code>mcp</code> group is unpaused:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get mcp -o json | jq -r '[\"MCP\",\"Paused\"], [\"---\",\"------\"], (.items[] | [(.metadata.name), (.spec.paused)]) | @tsv' | grep -v worker"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"MCP     Paused\n---     ------\nmaster  false\nmcp-1   false\nmcp-2   true"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      As each <code>mcp</code> group is upgraded, continue to unpause and upgrade the remaining nodes.
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get nodes"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME           STATUS                        ROLES                  AGE    VERSION\nctrl-plane-0   Ready                         control-plane,master   5d8h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nctrl-plane-1   Ready                         control-plane,master   5d8h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nctrl-plane-2   Ready                         control-plane,master   5d8h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nworker-0       Ready                         mcp-1,worker           5d8h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nworker-1       NotReady,SchedulingDisabled   mcp-2,worker           5d8h   v1.27.15+6147456"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <h2 id="update-verifying-the-health-of-the-newly-updated-cluster_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="group scroll-mt-20">Verifying the health of the newly updated cluster<a href="#update-verifying-the-health-of-the-newly-updated-cluster_completing-the-y-stream-update" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">After updating the cluster, verify that the cluster is back up and running.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Check the cluster version by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get clusterversion"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME      VERSION   AVAILABLE   PROGRESSING   SINCE   STATUS\nversion   4.16.14   True        False         4h38m   Cluster version is 4.16.14"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <p>This should return the new cluster version and the <code>PROGRESSING</code> column should return <code>False</code>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Check that all nodes are ready:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get nodes"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME           STATUS   ROLES                  AGE    VERSION\nctrl-plane-0   Ready    control-plane,master   5d9h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nctrl-plane-1   Ready    control-plane,master   5d9h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nctrl-plane-2   Ready    control-plane,master   5d9h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nworker-0       Ready    mcp-1,worker           5d9h   v1.29.8+f10c92d\nworker-1       Ready    mcp-2,worker           5d9h   v1.29.8+f10c92d"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <p>All nodes in the cluster should be in a <code>Ready</code> status and running the same version.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Check that there are no paused <code>mcp</code> resources in the cluster:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get mcp -o json | jq -r '[\"MCP\",\"Paused\"], [\"---\",\"------\"], (.items[] | [(.metadata.name), (.spec.paused)]) | @tsv' | grep -v worker"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"MCP     Paused\n---     ------\nmaster  false\nmcp-1   false\nmcp-2   false"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Check that all cluster Operators are available:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get co"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                                       VERSION   AVAILABLE   PROGRESSING   DEGRADED   SINCE   MESSAGE\nauthentication                             4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nbaremetal                                  4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\ncloud-controller-manager                   4.16.14   True        False         False      5d10h\ncloud-credential                           4.16.14   True        False         False      5d10h\ncluster-autoscaler                         4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nconfig-operator                            4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nconsole                                    4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\ncontrol-plane-machine-set                  4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\ncsi-snapshot-controller                    4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\ndns                                        4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\netcd                                       4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nimage-registry                             4.16.14   True        False         False      85m\ningress                                    4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\ninsights                                   4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nkube-apiserver                             4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nkube-controller-manager                    4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nkube-scheduler                             4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nkube-storage-version-migrator              4.16.14   True        False         False      4h48m\nmachine-api                                4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nmachine-approver                           4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nmachine-config                             4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nmarketplace                                4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nmonitoring                                 4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nnetwork                                    4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nnode-tuning                                4.16.14   True        False         False      5d7h\nopenshift-apiserver                        4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nopenshift-controller-manager               4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nopenshift-samples                          4.16.14   True        False         False      5h24m\noperator-lifecycle-manager                 4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\noperator-lifecycle-manager-catalog         4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\noperator-lifecycle-manager-packageserver   4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nservice-ca                                 4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h\nstorage                                    4.16.14   True        False         False      5d9h"} lang="terminal" title="Example output" />
      <p>All cluster Operators should report <code>True</code> in the <code>AVAILABLE</code> column.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Check that all pods are healthy:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc get po -A | grep -E -iv 'complete|running'"} lang="terminal" />
      <p>This should not return any pods.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>You might see a few pods still moving after the update. Watch this for a while to make sure all pods are cleared.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      </ol>
